'''

TODOs
-----
* [TUPLE1] Tuples should allow one field; more natural than singleton unions.
  * I'm not sure; it's simpler to simply lift than to wrap in sequence then lift
    which is how tuple construction works (and how its rendered).
  * Still, I see no reason to disallow it.
* [ACCESSORS] Auto-define tuple field accessors by putting names in the defn.
* [TOP] TOP domain
* Predefined domains, perhaps replacing base domains?
  * Z = integers
  * N = natural numbers?
  * S = strings of Unicode code points?
  * C = Unicode code point?
* For union types `U = A+B`, autogenerate:
  * lifting function `inU()`
  * lowering functions `U->A()` and `U->B()`
* For tuple types, autogenerate `mkDom` constructor.
* Typecase to safely and completely lower a union domain value
  * Similar seqcase to traverse sequences
* Ensure Union domains are fully disjoint, even when inlining nested Unions.
  * This makes indirect lowering unambiguous.
  * BUT: it will break current Ion modeling since each type is (+ DotNull ...)
* [CONST] Domain constants `(val <name> <expr>)`
  * Either print definition as part of the model, or inline them where used.
* Improve error reporting locations; TCE + PCS = no meaningful stack
  * I wish I could override `#%app`!
* Delay and memoize component domains (enable recursive types)
  * Allows the author to arrange domains arbitrarily, controlling the order in
    the document.
* `lift` and `lower` should statically detect impossible steps after the first.


Requires Fusion features:
* We need `with_output_to_string` in a non-private library.
* Better `display` of domains and values.
* [GUARD] Use record constructor guards to type-check values and supply defaults.


DSL Dialect
-----------
* [PROVIDE] `define_model` should `provide` the things it defines.
* Need [CONST] to get rid of `define` uses.
* [LET] Functional, strict let and letrec forms. (See L.I.S.P. p172)
  * Would trap Bottom as soon as it arises, even if the variable is usused.


Printer
-------
* It's not great that printer config needs to use "internal" names like `IF`.
  This may be unavoidable due to the phase-shifting between the DSL and model
  features and normal Fusion bindings for the print methods.
  * Perhaps can be fixed by having all models inherit from a base, then having
    the print-config clauses lookup fn/dom bindings separately.


Denoters
--------

Denoter function must cover all inputs.
Opaque denoter can just type-check
Everything is a function!

What do we want a denoter to do?
* Have input type  -- form of match-cases based on domain type (union vs product vs tuple)
* have output type
* apply
  - type-check inputs upon receipt
  - type-check results before return

'''

(define_fn (E (v RVal) (r Environment) -> Value)
  (case v (Symbolic "foo")))


(define_denoter (Ev [RVal] Environment::r Continuation::k -> 'Value*')
  '''
Resolves symbols in a single raw value.
  '''
  (match
    [RSym::sym]    (k r (lift (symbolize r sym) Symbol))    // E[[sym]]rk = k r symbolize(r sym)
    [RStruct::str] (k r (new_struct))
    [RList::l]     ('Ev*' (lower_to 'RVal*' l) r
                     (Continuation (r1 vs)
                       (k r1 (lift vs 'RList'))))
    [SafeVal::s]   (k r (lift s Value))))
'''
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
This is syntax in   This is "real code" as in define_fn
define_denoter


HARD: type-check match patterns at compile time if they recurse!
'''

(define_fn (Ev RVal::rv Environment::r Continuation::k -> 'Value*')
  (assert (is_union_domain RVal))
  (lets [(subdomain (domain_value_domain (domain_value_rep rv))),
         (subvalue  (lower_to subdomain rv)),
         (subfn     (case
                      ((ident subdomain RSym)    Ev_Rsym   )
                      ((ident subdomain RStruct) Ev_RStruct)
                      ((ident subdomain RList)   Ev_Rlist  )
                      ((ident subdomain SafeVal) Ev_SafeVal)
                      (true (wrong ...))))]
      (subfn subvalue r k)))

'''
Factoring out new top-level functions will make it easier to debug, I think.

    Name mangled      First arg lowered to one "match pattern" type
           vvvvvvv  vvvvvvvvv
'''
(define_fn Ev_RSym (RSym::sym Environment::r Continuation::k -> 'Value*')
  (k r (lift (symbolize r sym) Symbol)))
(define_fn Ev_RStruct
  ...)
(define_fn Ev (RVal::rv Environment::r Continuation::k -> 'Value*')
  (...))


(define_denoter ('Ev*' 'RVal*'::rvs Environment::r Continuation::k -> 'Value*')
  '''
Resolves symbols in a sequence of raw values.
  '''
  (match rvs
    []                        (k r <>)
    [RVal::rv1, 'RVal*'::rvs] (Ev rv1 r
                               (Continuation (r1 vs1)
                                 ('Ev*' r1
                                   (Continuation (r2 vs2)
                                     (k r2 (append vs1 vs2))))))))


(define_denoter ('Etop*' 'TopVal*' Env Cont -> Value*) ...)


(Etop* ( make TopVal* ... )   Env0 Cont0)
